{"study_accession":"PRJNA326471","secondary_study_accession":"SRP076902","title":"Dysregulated immune system networks in war veterans with PTSD","description":"Purpose: RNA-Seq analysis can help identify large set of differentially expressed genes at a time. We performed RNA-Seq analysis to identify differentially expressed genes in the PBMCs of war veterans suffering from PTSD. Methods: Total RNA from PBMCs from PTSD +ve and -ve individuals were used for RNA-Seq analysis. Results: We obtained, on average, ~60 millions reads per sample. More than 70% of the reads were mapped to human genome. Functional analysis of the differentially expressed genes (362) revealed dysregulation in immune system network. Conclusions: Our present study provides further proof that immune system related genes and pathways are dysregulated in PTSD PBMCs. Overall design: RNA-Seq was performed with RNA from 5 each control and PTSD individuals. PBMCs collected within one hour of blood draw were used for RNA isolation. 1 ug of total RNA was used for library synthesis and sequenced in a HighSeq 2000 illumina instrument at Tufts University.","pubmed":"27510991;28850112","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN05278180","study_accession":"PRJNA326471","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Control1","description":"Control1","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM2210776","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2017-11-09","attributes":[["source_name","PBMCs"],["group","PTSD -ve"],["tissue","Peripheral blood"],["age","Mean 42.6 years"],["genotype","not applicable"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR3709488","experiment_accession":"SRX1869632","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2000","read_count":73036090,"base_count":3724840590,"first_public":"2017-11-09","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2000 sequencing: GSM2210776: Control1 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN05278181","study_acc